\description{
Predicts the fraction unbound of a compound in an incubation with
microsomes or cells, such as hepatocytes. Two kinds of method are available:
\itemize{
\item literature regressions on lipophilicity (\code{austin}, \code{hallifax}, \code{turner},
\code{kilford}, \code{poulin}, and their average \code{all_literature}), which need only
the compound properties and the microsome or cell concentration;
\item partition models (\code{poulin_theil}, \code{berezhkovskiy}, \code{pksim_standard},
\code{rodgers_rowland}, \code{schmitt}), which describe binding to the lipids and
proteins of the cells or microsomes, to serum in the medium and to the
plastic of the well. They also need the serum fraction, the microplate
type and the medium volume.
}
}
\details{
A strong base is a compound whose first ionization class is \code{"base"} with
a pKa above 7.

\code{"berezhkovskiy"} and \code{"berezhkovskiy_fu"} currently give the same results
as \code{"poulin_theil"} and \code{"poulin_theil_fu"}.
}
